    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (69.90). **Jackson Merrill** stands out as the premier play; his matchup against Yesavage is bolstered by a potent combination of a 13% platoon edge and a strong spot in the two-hole, maximizing his opportunities to rack up counting stats. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a 16% park factor boost, allowing him to overcome the standard penalty associated with his left-handed platoon split. **Kyle Tucker** (69.76) and **Andy Pages** (65.76) also present formidable floors against Pfaadt, with **Andy Pages** specifically flagged for a 2% boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which may provide the necessary window to capitalize on our league\u2019s premium on stolen bases.\n\nWhile the lineup is optimized for efficiency, the decision to leave **Miguel Vargas** on the bench (52.17) was the tightest call of the morning. Although **Miguel Vargas** possesses an elite 0.398 xwOBA, his score was suppressed by the opposing catcher\u2019s quick pop time and an elite pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners, making him less viable in our SB-centric scoring structure compared to the high-floor reliability of **Josh Jung** (56.77) or **Drake Baldwin** (56.39). We must exercise caution with **Drake Baldwin**, however, as a 32% rain risk introduces significant volatility to his outlook. Furthermore, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.87) is locked in, his score remains slightly muted by a negative platoon adjustment against Buehler, emphasizing the need for **Jacob Wilson** (58.81) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.38) to set the table effectively at the top of the order to compensate for any potential mid-game weather disruptions.",
